    "description": "Designed, developed and implemented cash reversal ticketing as part of a new product for World Bank, Bloomberg largest and most important repo client. This new functionality was offered as part of a new product release for all repo clients.\nMigrated all repo/cash servers/services to Jenkins continuous integration platform which increased team projects efficiency by 30%.\nConverted repo/cash data from legacy internal COMDB databases to current internal COMDB2 databases, improving team servers efficiency in retrieving and saving critical repo/collateral related data thus increased the overall customer satisfaction in repo/collateral Bloomberg online functions response time.\nCoordinated with QA testers for end-to-end unit testing and pre-production testing for both new and existing online and offline builds which eliminated potential issues in production.\nCollaborated on the design and creation of company first block/allocation matching engine via FIX which led to the creation of a new paid client tier, AIM premium.\nImplemented extensive business logic for the block and allocation matching/affirmation workflows which directly improved clients' trades settlement successes thus minimizing their costs.\nOrganized a team of programmers to create a new printed tickets server which added the new printed tickets in Kanji to the existing support in English resulting in an improvement in efficiency of the clients' backoffice operations in Japan. \nMigrated all the servers within the team from sister machine backup system to SAT compatible configuration while mentoring 80% of the team members on middle office operations when team was in transition to new management.\nEnhanced and maintained the complete middle office post trade processing workflow end-to-end services including matching, custody and trade feeds to clients' backoffice.",
